    {
      "field_name": "timecourse_subsequent",
      "value": "chronic-progressive",
      "quote": "In January 2013, she developed painful muscle cramps of the arms and generalized muscle rigidity with cervical involvement, and was bedridden. Based on clinical symptoms, SPS was diagnosed and the patient was treated with corticosteroids (500 mg IV/3 d), followed by PLEX/IA (5 sessions). Antispastic medication with baclofen and diazepam was started. In the following months, symptoms gradually improved, and after rehabilitation the patient was able to walk some steps.",
      "confidence": "medium"
    },
